The DTM Data Service, previously released as a Public Preview, is now generally available. The microservice processes data point links configured through the DTM [Data Points plugin](/dtm/asset-hierarchy/#datapoints) and automatically propagates incoming device measurements to the corresponding assets in the digital twin hierarchy through `c8y_LinkedSeries`. As soon as a data point link is created in DTM, the service starts forwarding incoming measurements from the source device to the linked data point on the asset.

This makes operational data available directly on assets, so you can build asset-centric dashboards, analytics, smart rules, and business applications without querying individual devices. The number of measurements created on assets depends on how many assets a device measurement is linked to. For example, if a device measurement is linked to three assets, the DTM Data Service creates three measurements on the asset level for each incoming device measurement.

{{< c8y-admon-info >}}
The DTM Data Service is not enabled by default. To enable it for your tenant, contact [{{< product-c8y-iot >}} support](/additional-resources/contacting-support).
{{< /c8y-admon-info >}}
